course: dictionary
lesson: 2263
title: Words that describe food and colour
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Creamy has two main meanings. The first is thick, smooth and rich, like cream or food that has a lot of cream in it. The second is a pale, yellowish-white colour, like cream itself. Look at the words around creamy to find out which meaning the writer means.
explain: «Egg yolk can keep the droplets apart for good: its molecules have one end that likes water and one that likes oil, which is how thick, creamy mayonnaise is made.» Thick is a clue. Mayonnaise is a food, so creamy describes how it feels to eat, not its colour.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try "thick, smooth and rich mayonnaise". It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning. If the sentence is about paint or a wall, the colour meaning is more likely.
fact: Creamy means thick, smooth and rich, like cream.
fact: Creamy can also mean pale yellowish-white in colour, like cream.
fact: Creamy is often used for soups, yoghurt, ice cream and sauces: «creamy texture» and «smooth and creamy».
fact: Creamy is the adjective. Its comparative forms are creamier and creamiest.
fact: Texture is how something feels or looks when you touch or taste it. Creamy describes a texture that is smooth and not grainy.
exercise: «Egg yolk can keep the droplets apart for good, which is how thick, creamy mayonnaise is made.» What does creamy mean in this sentence? | Crunchy and dry | Cold and icy | *Thick and smooth, like cream | Sharp and sour
exercise: «The walls were a soft, creamy white.» What colour does creamy suggest here? | *Pale yellowish-white | Deep purple | Shiny black | Bright green
exercise: The yoghurt was smooth and creamy. Which words could replace creamy and keep the same meaning? | *Thick and smooth | Hard and crumbly | Dry and grainy | Sharp and sour
test: «Her ice cream was rich and creamy.» What does creamy mean here? | Covered in crunchy nuts | Sour and sharp | Frozen solid | *Thick, smooth and rich
test: Which of these is a creamy texture? | A crisp apple | A sharp lemon | A rough stone | *A smooth, thick sauce
exam: Which word means the same as creamy when it describes a texture? | Bitter | Spiky | Crunchy | *Smooth and thick
